    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/952802?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in Experimental and Computational Fracture Mechanics",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in Experimental and Computational Fracture Mechanics kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in Experimental and Computational Fracture Mechanics School of Engineering Sciences at KTH Job description The position focus on experimental and computational fracture mechanics. A central issue in the work includes experimental testing of mini-CT specimens combined with numerical modeling. The main objective is to improve existing methods for characterizing crack growth resistance in ductile materials. Use of sub-sized specimens in assessment of structural integrity is an area under strong development and includes issues such as geometry effects as well as transferability of laboratory results to actual components. The outcome of the project is foreseen to be an integrated testing and computational methodology that can be standardized according to regulatory perspectives. You will work in a research environment together with other researchers focused on material and fracture mechanics problems related to metals of interest to the process industry, where parts of the project will be carried out in collaboration with the Swedish nuclear industry. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. In addition to your scientific skills and pedagogical ability, a relevant doctoral thesis, international experience and proficiency in English as it is needed in the daily work Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline Experience in mechanical testing Good knowledge and skill in nonlinear computational mechanics Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality Collaborative abilities Independence Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2559 Published 02.Jul.2026 Last application date 07.Sep.2026 Contact Jonas Faleskog +4687908977 faleskog@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/962756?l=en": {
      "title": "Research Engineer in Robotic Hardware and Mechanical Design",
      "description": "KTH | Research Engineer in Robotic Hardware and Mechanical Design kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Research Engineer in Robotic Hardware and Mechanical Design KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences Job description In this role, you develop, integrate, and test hardware for autonomous robots, focusing on mechanical design, electronics, embedded systems, and prototyping. Tasks include CAD, sensors, actuators, power, wiring, and PCB development. You interface the hardware with ROS2 and verify it in simulation and the field; Python/C++ is used mainly for bring-up, testing, and integration. The position is part of I-SEE – Integrated Aerial–Surface–Subsurface Autonomy for Extreme Environments , which aims to reduce weather dependency, costs, and safety risks in marine AUV operations through AI-enabled autonomous launch and recovery. It links aerial, surface, and underwater vehicles. You will focus on physical platforms and mechanical/electrical subsystems for edge perception, distributed decision-making, operator support, and robust operation in demanding environments. Based at KTH's Department of Engineering Mechanics, the role includes fabrication, assembly, troubleshooting, documentation, and lab/field trials. You will work with researchers, engineers, and external partners through design reviews, prototyping, testing, and iterative development. Qualifications Requirements A graduate degree in advanced level (higher education) in mechanical engineering, mechatronics, electrical engineering, engineering design, or another relevant field. Experience with embedded hardware or systems, including integration of electronics, sensors, actuators, motors, or power. Very good Python and/or C++ skills and practical ROS2 experience, especially for testing, bring-up, and hardware integration. Experience with hands-on testing and integration work in laboratory or field environments. Good ability to communicate in spoken and written English, as it is required in the day to day work. Availability to travel within Sweden and Europe. Ability to swim. In the evaluation, we will consider: Expertise in mechanical design and electronics Ability to design, integrate, and test robust robotic hardware Ability to work safely and methodically in workshop, lab, and field settings Ability to solve interdisciplinary design problems and document technical solutions Collaboration skills Ability to work independently Personal skills You are self-driven, solution-oriented, and meticulous, and enjoy moving between CAD, electronics/PCB work, assembly, troubleshooting, and field testing. You collaborate well and contribute to a positive, professional environment. Preferred qualifications Experience with drones, AUVs/ROVs, or other marine or mobile robots. Experience with vehicles, boats, or practical field operations in relevant environments (inc. relevant licences). Mechanical design and CAD, including dimensioning, materials, and manufacturing documentation. Electronics and PCB design, including schematics, layout, bring-up, and troubleshooting. 3D printing or other prototyping methods and Unity or another simulation environment. Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application should include: CV, including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of degree certificate(s) and transcripts from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish are required if the original documents are not issued in either of these languages. A brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests, and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals (max. 2 pages). Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to 12 months, with access according to agreement. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2854 Published 26.Aug.2026 Last application date 11.Sep.2026 Contact Ivan Stenius stenius@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/943642?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in Infection Biophysics and Microengineering",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student in Infection Biophysics and Microengineering kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student in Infection Biophysics and Microengineering School of Engineering Sciences at KTH Project description Third-cycle subject: Biological Physics The Hannebelle Lab at the Division of Biophysics, Department of Applied Physics, studies the physical mechanisms of infection. We are based at KTH and SciLifeLab in Stockholm ( https://hannebellelab.org/ ). We are seeking a PhD student to study the biophysics of schistosome skin infection. Schistosomiasis affects over 200 million people worldwide and is among the most prevalent neglected tropical diseases. Infection begins when schistosome parasites penetrate intact human skin from freshwater, a multi-hour process that remains largely uncharacterized in biophysical terms. Using in-vivo-mimetic systems, this project will investigate how these parasites find, penetrate, migrate through, and exit the skin, and what physical mechanisms govern each step. The work is highly interdisciplinary, bringing together microfluidics and organ-on-chip platforms, custom microscopy, cell culture, 3D printing and hardware design, and biophysical modeling. We do not expect applicants to arrive with expertise in all of these. What matters most is a demonstrated ability to learn new methods, a willingness to work across disciplines, and genuine curiosity about how physical principles shape biological processes. We are a young research group with a bold scientific vision, committed to supporting each member's growth into a skilled and independent researcher. You will join us at SciLifeLab in Solna. Supervision: Martin Viklund and Melanie Hannebelle is proposed to supervise the doctoral student. Decisions are made on admission Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge The applicant should preferably have a Master’s degree in infection biology, biophysics, applied physics, biotechnology, biomedical engineering, or a closely related field. In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach and analyze and work with complex issues. The project is highly interdisciplinary: microfluidics, cell culture, parasite handling, custom microscopy, 3D printing, and biophysical modeling. Prior experience in some of these is valued, but not expected in all. Above all, we look for a demonstrated ability and enthusiasm to learn new methods. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages.Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment 1 October 2026 Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2149 Published 03.Sep.2026 Last application date 12.Sep.2026 Contact Melanie Hannebelle melanieh@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/949568?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral Student in Electromagnetics",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral Student in Electromagnetics kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral Student in Electromagnetics KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Project description Third-cycle subject: Electrical Engineering We are seeking a doctoral student for research in electromagnetic scattering, radar cross-section (RCS) analysis, and periodic electromagnetic structures, with applications to radar signatures of unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs). Supervision: Oscar Quevedo-Teruel is proposed to supervise the doctoral student. Decisions are made on admission Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge. The applicant should hold a degree at the advanced level in Electrical Engineering, Engineering Physics, Physics, or a related field. The applicant should have a strong background in electromagnetic theory, wave propagation, and mathematical modeling. In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach, analyze and work with complex issues, knowledge of electromagnetic scattering and radar cross-section (RCS) analysis, experience with physical optics or other high-frequency electromagnetic techniques, experience with periodic electromagnetic structures, metasurfaces, or frequency-selective surfaces, experience with electromagnetic simulation tools such as CST Microwave Studio, Ansys HFSS, or COMSOL Multiphysics, programming skills in MATLAB, Python, or similar environments, Experience with antenna or electromagnetic measurements. strong scientific communication skills and proficiency in Swedish, both written and spoken, is considered a merit as this is needed in the daily work. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages.Copies of originals must be certified . A curriculum vitae (CV), including relevant education, professional experience, research activities, technical skills, and other qualifications relevant to the position. The CV must not exceed two pages. A motivation letter describing why you wish to pursue doctoral studies, your academic and research interests, and how these relate to your previous studies, experience, and future career goals. The letter must not exceed two pages. Up to two representative publications, theses, project reports, or technical reports demonstrating your research capabilities. For longer documents, please provide an abstract and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment 1st October 2026 according to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2423 Published 03.Sep.2026 Last application date 12.Sep.2026 Contact Oscar Quevedo Teruel oscarqt@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/960383?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in Multiomics Machine Learning Cancer Bioinformatics",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student in Multiomics Machine Learning Cancer Bioinformatics kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student in Multiomics Machine Learning Cancer Bioinformatics KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences in Chemistry, Biotechnology and Health Project description Third-cycle subject: BIO Biotechnology – Cancer Bioinformatics We are looking for a motivated PhD student to join our lab at KTH/SciLifeLab in Stockholm, where we focus on precision medicine, cancer progression, and the tumor microenvironment. This project aims to investigate factors contributing to tumor progression and their links to cancer progression, particularly in genitourinary cancers. The project will involve bioinformatics-driven analyses, multi-omics data integration using machine learning, and potential collaborations with clinical and translational researchers. The project is well-suited for candidates with a background in bioinformatics, computational biology, machine learning with particular experience with cancer biology, or a related field. Supervision: Assist Prof. Arian Lundberg and Prof. Cecilia Williams are proposed to supervise the doctoral student. Decisions are made on admission Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge Strong background in cancer biology. Master’s degree in bioinformatics, Computational Biology, or related fields is required. Proficiency in Bash, R, and/or Python is essential for data analysis and multiomics integration, and bioinformatics tasks. Ability to work independently and in a collaborative team environment is essential. Strong communication skills for presenting findings and working with others, in English is required. Two references from previous academic or research teams are required, one of which shall be your previous supervisor. In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently drive their work forward, collaborate with others, have a professional approach, and analyze and work with complex issues. strong problem-solving abilities and attention to detail. ability to work independently, take initiative, and manage multiple tasks simultaneously. experience in interdisciplinary research and an interest in collaborating with researchers from different fields. good understanding of scientific literature and the ability to understand and analyze complex information. experience with machine learning and multiomics data integration. skills in additional programming languages, bioinformatics pipelines, or tools are an advantage. experience working with clinical or cancer patient data is advantageous. experience with High Performance Computing (HPC) is an advantage. a solid background in cancer research is preferred. good communication skills in English, both written and spoken, as required in the daily work. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages.Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2755 Published 03.Sep.2026 Last application date 12.Sep.2026 Contact Arian Lundberg arian.lundberg@scilifelab.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
