    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/953991?l=en": {
      "title": "Technician to KTH / Energy Technology",
      "description": "KTH | Technician to KTH / Energy Technology kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Technician to KTH / Energy Technology KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Industrial Engineering and Management Do you enjoy practical work with mechanical manufacturing and laboratory activities? We are looking for a technician for the Department of Energy Technology, where you will build prototypes and test rigs to support experimental research and education. We warmly welcome your application!. About the department/group The position is based at the Division of Applied Thermodynamics and Refrigeration within the Department of Energy Technology. The work is conducted in a creative and dynamic environment, which involves close collaboration with many industrial partners, other technical staff, laboratory managers, researchers, doctoral students, and undergraduate students. The division is globally known for research in the field of heat pump and refrigeration systems. Job description The tasks primarily involve supporting our experimental and laboratory activities. The position includes the following tasks and responsibilities: Mechanical manufacturing (lathe, milling, welding, brazing, etc.). Construction of prototypes and test rigs, commissioning, and technical support. Design support for experimental research and education projects in collaboration with researchers and doctoral students (including the assessment of design drawings for external production). Purchasing support. Participation in the development of risk assessments. Acting as fire safety responsible (training via employer) and chemical responsible person, in collaboration with colleagues. Service and maintenance of the lab and workshop infrastructure. Qualifications Requirements At least upper secondary education in mechanics or equivalent. Basic knowledge in 3-phase electricity. Basic knowledge of English, as this will be required in day-to-day work. Work experience with refrigeration, heat pumps, and thermal energy systems. Personal qualities We are looking for someone who is generally handy and has an interest in energy-related topics. You are creative, have strong collaborative skills, and work with independence and flexibility in a dynamic work environment. Preferred qualifications Work experience in electricity. Work experience with the building of prototypes. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. As an applicant, you are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete when submitted and that the qualifications we request in the advertisement are clearly stated in your CV. In this recruitment, you apply with your CV only. Instead of a cover letter, you will be asked to answer one or more questions in the recruitment system. It is important that you answer the questions carefully and truthfully, so that we can gain a clear understanding of your skills and experience. We base our selection on the qualifications outlined in the advertisement. Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid until further notice (permanent post) according to agreement. The employment begins with a six-month probationary period. Other information Striving towards gender equality, diversity and equal conditions is both a question of quality for KTH and a given part of our values. For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. Tests may be used in this recruitment process. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence Apply here Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2615 Published 08.Jul.2026 Last application date 30.Sep.2026 Contact Hatef Madani hatef.madani@energy.kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/949190?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in AI and Robotics for Production",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student in AI and Robotics for Production kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student in AI and Robotics for Production KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Industrial Engineering and Management Project description Third-cycle subject: Production engineering We are seeking a motivated PhD student in intelligent robotics for production, with a focus on robot learning and AI-enabled automation. The research aims to develop intelligent robotic systems that combine learning-based methods and advanced algorithms to support flexible, adaptive and human-centred industrial production. The work includes reinforcement learning, foundation models, world models and dexterous manipulation with applications in real industrial environments. The PhD student will collaborate closely with leading researchers, industrial partners, and international collaborators, contributing to both scientific advances and industrial innovation. The position is part of the Center of Excellence for Production Research (XPRES) and includes collaboration with leading European universities. The doctoral student will also join the new Production Systems and Automation unit at KTH, an inclusive and internationally oriented environment for research in intelligent robotics and automation for future production systems. We welcome applicants with diverse backgrounds and perspectives. Supervision: Xi Wang och Sichao Liu is proposed to supervise the doctoral student. Decisions are made on admission Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach and analyze and work with complex issues. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. In the case of studies that are to be completed with a licentiate degree, the total period of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education for two years. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages.Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2398 Published 03.Sep.2026 Last application date 01.Oct.2026 Contact Xi Wang wangxi@kth.se Magnus Wiktorsson magwik@kth.se Sichao Liu sicliu@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
